.TH CAT 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
cat \- concatenate files and print them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cat
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cat
writes the contents of each
.I file
to standard output, one after another.
With no
.IR file ,
or where a
.I file
is
.BR \- ,
it reads standard input.
.PP
Each read takes what the file has now and writes it at once, so a file that
never ends (a sensor's,
.BR /dev/motion0 :
an event a line) shows each piece as it comes.
.PP
A file that cannot be opened or read is reported on standard error, and
.B cat
goes on with the next one.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every file was read; 1 if any could not be opened or read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cat notes.txt
cat head.txt \- tail.txt > all.txt
cat /dev/motion0
.fi
.SH NOTES
GNU
.BR cat 's
options (\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-A\fR and the others) are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR head (1),
.BR tail (1),
.BR less (1)
